# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private operator source material for knowledge imports.
#
# Practitioner spreadsheets, protocol documents and Obsidian exports are the
# practitioner's own material and third-party copyrighted content. They are
# staged HERE, on the operator's machine, and never enter the repository.
#
# This is deliberately a wildcard directory rather than a list of filenames: a
# rule that has to be updated every time someone adds a file is a rule that
# eventually is not updated. Only the manifest, which contains hashes and
# mappings but no source content, is committed — and only when the operator
# copies it out to docs/ explicitly.
/private-import/**
# ...except the two files that carry no source content: the template operators
# copy, and the instructions for using it.
!/private-import/README.md
!/private-import/manifest.example.json

*.import-source.xlsx
*.import-source.csv
*.import-source.md

# Reviewed AWS deployment manifests contain account and operator identifiers.
/infra/aws-clinical-core/deployment-manifest.json
/infra/aws-clinical-core/synthetic-acceptance-manifest.json
/infra/aws-clinical-core/production-readiness.json
/infra/aws-clinical-core/first-real-data-pilot-readiness.json
/supabase/.temp/
